     [ 0.6   -0.333  1.   ]]
    [[5.    4.    2.   ]
     [0.    1.2   2.6  ]
     [0.    0.    0.667]]

    The original matrix can be reconstructed by multiplying the three together:

    >>> a_reconstructed = P @ L @ U
